{
  "_comment": "CloudCLI, the npm package @cloudcli-ai/cloudcli, installed per account with the module's own Node.js. The node artifact is the nodejs.org standalone build of Node.js 22 LTS at one pinned release for every version, unpacked under cloudcli/node without the archive's top directory; each digest is what nodejs.org/dist/v22.23.3/SHASUMS256.txt names, and npmmirror serves the same files. The cloudcli artifact is the npm package, fetched from the npm source set, its digest the integrity registry.npmjs.org gives the tested version; its hosts are the ones better-sqlite3's prebuild-install fetches its binary from, the GitHub release first. node-pty and bcrypt carry their binaries inside their npm packages.",
  "name": "cloudcli",
  "title": "CloudCLI",
  "description": "AI coding sessions in the browser, one per account, opened from a client with a token",
  "publisher": "siteboon/claudecodeui",
